"hadiths[176]{hadithnumber,text}:"
648,"It was narrated from Hazrat Rafa' bin Rafi' that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked, ""Which earning is more pure?"" He said: ""The earnings of a man's own hand and every kind of trade that is free from deceit and deceit."" (Narrated by Bazar and confirmed by Hakim)."
649,"It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah that he heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say in Makkah in the year of the conquest of Makkah: ""Indeed, Allah and His Messenger have forbidden the trade in wine, dead pigs, and idols."" He was asked: O Messenger of Allah! What do you say about dead animal fat? Because with it boats are gilded and hides are lubricated and people burn it for light. He said: ""No, that too is forbidden."" Then the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""May Allah spoil the Jews."" When Allah made fat forbidden to them, they melted it and sold it and ate its price."" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
650,"There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, who says: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: ""When there is a dispute between the seller and the buyer, and no one has evidence or testimony, then the owner of the property will be valid, or both of them should abandon the transaction."""
651,"It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Mas'ud Ansari that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog, the earnings of a wicked woman, and the sweets of a priest. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
652,"It is narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was traveling on one of his tired camels. He decided to leave her. It is narrated by Hazrat Jabir that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me from behind. You prayed for me and hit the camel and it started to run faster than it had ever run before. He said: ""Sell me this camel for one ounce of silver."" I said: No! He then said again: ""Sell me this camel."" So I sold it to you for one ounce of silver and stipulated that I would ride it to my family. So, as soon as I reached (Madinah), I took that camel and came to your service. You paid me the cash price for it.' Then I returned (after receiving the money) and you sent (a camel too) after me and said: 'Did you think about me that I lowered the price so that I could take your camel?' Take your camel and keep the money with you, so it is for you.” (Bukhari and Muslim) This context is in Muslim."
653,"On the authority of Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that one of us made his slave a slave. He had no wealth except this slave. The Prophet called this slave and sold him. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
654,"It is narrated from Hazrat Maimunah, the wife of the Prophet, that a mouse fell into ghee and died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about it, and he said: ""Take it out and throw it out and throw out the ghee around it and use (the remaining ghee)."""
655,"Hazrat Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""When a rat falls into ghee, if the ghee is frozen, throw out the rat and the ghee around it, and if the ghee is liquid, do not break even near it."""
656,"It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Zubayr (may Allah have mercy on him) that I asked Hazrat Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) about the price of a bat and a dog. (Muslim and Feminine) and Feminine has this addition: ""Except for a hunting dog."""
657,"It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said that Hazrat Barirah (the maid) came to me and said: I have written to my owners for nine (9) ounces of silver that I will continue to pay one ounce every year, so help me (in this matter). I said: If your owners like me to pay your total amount in one lump sum and your villa will be for me, then I am ready to do so. Hazrat Barirah (may Allah be pleased with her) went to her owners with this proposal and told them this, but they refused to accept it. Hazrat Berira (RA) came back to him. At that time, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was also present. Barira said: I made that proposal to my owners but they refused to accept it and they say that the villa will be for them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard this and Hazrat Aisha (RA) also informed the Prophet (PBUH) about this incident, so he said: ""Take him and make a condition of the villa with him, because the rightful owner of the villa is the one who gives freedom."" Hazrat Aisha did the same. After that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up to address the people. Praise be to Allah, the Exalted.” Then he said: “What has happened to the people that they impose such conditions that are not in the Book of Allah. (Remember that) every condition that is not in the Book of Allah is void, even if there are hundreds of conditions. Allah's judgment is very true and Allah's condition is very firm and firm. And the villa belongs to the one who frees. (Bukhari and Muslim. These words are Bukhari's. ) and the words of Muslim are that he said: ""Buy him and set him free and make a condition of a villa with him."" ""."
658,"There is a hadith on the authority of Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that Hazrat Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, forbade the sale of Umm-Wald and said: It cannot be sold, it cannot be gifted, nor can it be divided into inheritance. He can benefit from it as long as the owner wants and when the owner dies, he is free. (It has been narrated by Bayhaqi and Malik and they have said that some have called it Marfoo, which is an illusion.)"
659,"There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who says that we used to sell the women and children of slave girls in the presence of the Prophet (peace be upon him). You didn't see any ugliness in it. (Nasa’i, Ibn Majah, and Darqutni narrated it all three, and Ibn Hibban called it Sahih.)"
660,"There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of water in excess of what is needed. (Muslim) And there is this addition in a hadith: And you have also prohibited taking compensation for a pair of camels."
661,"On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the payment of a male mate. (Bukhari)"
662,"It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the marriage of Habal-Hablah. And this sale was in the period of Jahiliyyah (in this way) that a man would buy a camel on the condition that he would pay its price when the camel gave birth to a child, then the child in the camel's belly would give birth (to another child). (Bukhari and Muslim. And these words are Bukhari's)"
663,"It is also narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of a villa and its donation. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
664,"There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, who says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade trade by throwing pebbles and trade by deception. (Muslim)"
665,"On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever buys grain, he should not sell it (further) until he measures it."" (Muslim)"
666,"On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two pledges in one pledge. (It has been narrated by Ahmada and Nasa'i, and Tirmidhi and Ibn Hibban have declared it to be authentic.) And it is in the tradition of Abu Dawud: (The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said:) ""Whoever makes two deals in one deal, he will either get less or else he will take interest."""
667,"Hazrat Amr ibn Shuaib narrates from his father (Shuaib) and he (Shuaib) from his grandfather (Abdullah ibn Amr, may God be pleased with him) who says that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Loan and sale (together) are not lawful, nor are two conditions lawful in one sale."" And it is not permissible to profit from a thing before taking possession of it. And it is not permissible or halal to sell what you do not have. (This hadith has been narrated by Al-Tabarani in the same manner and it is poor.)"
668,"Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrates from his father (Shuaib) and he (Shuaib) from his grandfather (Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of Arabs. (It was narrated by Imam Malik, may God have mercy on him. And he said: I have received this tradition from Amr bin Shuaib.)"
669,"It is narrated from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: I bought oil (olive) from the market. When my deal was settled, I found a man who offered me a good profit. I decided to make a deal with this man.' Meanwhile, someone grabbed my arm from behind. I turned around and saw that it was Hazrat Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: Do not sell it at the place where you bought it, even if you carry it to your house, because the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling things from where they are bought, unless the merchants and traders take the purchased goods to their homes. (It was narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawud, and these words are Abu Dawud's, and Ibn Hibban and Hakim called it Sahih.)"
670,"On the authority of Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he says: I said: O Messenger of Allah! I trade camels in Baqi. I sell in dinars and receive dirhams and (sometimes) I sell in dirhams and receive dinars (ie) I take dinars in exchange for dirhams and give dirhams in exchange for dinars. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""There is no problem if you exchange them with your brother on the same day, and before you both separate from each other, no part of the money remains due to anyone."""
671,"On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade impurity. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
672,"It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the pledge of allegiance, Muzabnah, Mukhabara and Sanya, but in this case (Bay Sanya) is permissible if it is determined. (It has been narrated by all five except Ibn Majah and Tirmidhi has declared it Sahih.)"
673,"It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Anas, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade buying, selling, makhadira, mulamsa, manabza and muzabna. (Bukhari)"
674,"Hazrat Tawas narrates on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him. He says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Do not go ahead and meet the merchant caravans, and let no citizen sell the goods of a villager."" He said: Citizens should not become pimps of villagers. (Bukhari and Muslim. And these words are Bukhari's)"
675,"There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, who says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Do not go ahead and meet those who bring grain to the city from outside."" (The merchant) who was met on the way and bought his goods, after reaching the market, the owner of the goods (the merchant) has the right (whether to keep the deal or to cancel it) (Muslim)."
676,"It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Hurairah that he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a citizen to sell the goods of a villager. And (said): ""If you do not intend to buy a deal, do not raise the price."" And no one should marry his brother's marriage, nor should he marry his brother's marriage. And no woman should demand the divorce of her (Muslim) sister in order to get what is her share."
677,"There is a hadith on the authority of Abu Ayyub Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: ""Whoever separates a mother from her child, Allah will separate her and her loved ones on the Day of Resurrection."""
678,"On the authority of Hazrat Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to sell two slave brothers. I sold them both to separate men and then I mentioned it to you, so you said: ""Go and bring them back and sell them both together."""
679,"It is narrated from Hazrat Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that he says that during the reign of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, the prices of things rose in Madinah. People said: O Messenger of Allah! The prices of commodities have become (big) fast, you fix (their) prices for us. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Allah is the One who determines the price, He is the one who restricts, the one who gives generously, and the one who provides."" I want that when I meet Allah Ta'ala, no one will ask me for life and wealth on the grounds of oppression."
680,"There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Muammar bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who narrates from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “No one hoards except a sinner.” (Muslim)"
681,"Hazrat Abu Huraira (RA) narrates from the Prophet (PBUH) that he said: ""(When selling) do not stop the milk of camels and sheep in their udders. If a person buys such an animal, after milking it, he has the right to choose the better of two things, whether he keeps the animal and if he wants to return it with a saa of dates."" (Bukhari and Muslim) And in the tradition of Muslim, it is: ""He has the right for three days."" Imam Bukhari, may God have mercy on him, states that dates are mentioned in most hadiths."
682,"It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that whoever buys a goat whose milk has stopped in its udders, and then returns it, then he should return one Sa'a with it. (Bukhari) and Ismaili have narrated the addition that one saa is dates."
683,"It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a pile of grain. As you inserted your hand into it, your fingers felt moist. He said: ""O owner of grains! What is this?'' He said: O Messenger of Allah! It had rained on him. He said: ""Then why did you not put it (moistened part) on top of the grain so that the (buyers) could see it?"" Whoever cheated has nothing to do with me.” (Muslim)"
684,"Hazrat Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from his father Hazrat Burida (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever withholds the grapes during their harvest to sell them to a winemaker will enter Hellfire knowingly.”"
685,"It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The one who is entitled to the income is the one who is the guarantor."""
686,"It is narrated from Hazrat Urwa Baraqi (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) gave him one dinar to buy a sacrificial animal or a goat. He bought two goats for one dinar, then sold one of them for one dinar and came to your service with one goat and one dinar. You prayed for them to be blessed in their trade, so they were like that even if they bought soil, they would definitely get profit from it too. (All five of them have narrated it, except Nasa'i, and Imam Bukhari, may God have mercy on him, narrated it in the context of a hadith, but he did not quote these words, and Tirmidhi narrated the hadith narrated by Hazrat Hakim bin Hizam, may God be pleased with him, as a witness for him.)"
687,"On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade buying the babies of animals before they were born, and forbade buying the milk (collected) in their udders, and forbade the buying of a runaway slave, and forbade the buying of booty before it was distributed, and forbade the buying of alms before it was seized, and forbade the purchase of a diver’s dive (in advance). (It was narrated by Ibn Majah, Bazar and Darqutni with a weak chain of transmission.)"
688,"It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Do not buy the fish in the water, for it is deceitful."""
689,"It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade the sale of fruits before they are (ripe and) edible, and also forbade the sale of wool on the backs of animals and milk in the udders. (This hadith was narrated by Tabarani in his middle and by Darqutani. And Abu Dawud narrated it in Ikrima’s Murasil and this is Rajih. Also, it was narrated by Abu Dawud with a strong chain of transmission from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, and Bayhaqi preferred it.)"
690,"It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the buying and selling of articles and medicines. (It was narrated by Bazar and its chain of transmission is weak.)"
691,"On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever returns the goods sold from a Muslim, Allah will forgive his sins and misdeeds.”"
692,"Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) that he said: ""When two men begin to bargain with each other, each of them has authority until they stay together and do not separate from each other"" or they give authority to each other. If one ""gives authority to the other"" and then the deal is settled on it, then the deal is complete. And if they separate from each other after making the deal, and neither of them has canceled the pledge, then the pledge will be valid.” (Bukhari and Muslim. These words are from Muslim)"
693,"Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrated from his father (Shuaib) from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The buyer and the seller have authority until they separate"" unless the transaction is an authority. And it is not permissible to leave hastily because of the fear of returning the bargain.”"
694,"It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) that a person was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) that he was usually cheated in marriage. He (called him) and said: ""When making a deal, say that there will be no deception."" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
695,"It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (SAW) cursed the usury taker, the giver, the person who wrote it and its witnesses, and said: “All of them are equal and equal (in the commission of sin).”"
696,"Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrates from the Prophet (PBUH) that he said: “There are seventy-three levels of usury. The lowest degree is like the sin of a man marrying his own mother. And above all usury is to disgrace a Muslim."
697,"Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, narrated that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Do not sell gold for gold, but equal."" Do not add to each other's weight. And do not sell silver for silver, but equal, and do not add to each other's weight. And do not sell the loan in exchange for cash.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
698,"On the authority of Hazrat Ubada bin Samit, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, and salt for salt, equally and in cash. If there is a difference in the goods, then sell as you wish, provided that (the exchange of goods on both sides) is in cash."" (Muslim)"
699,"On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Exchange gold for gold (when it is equal in weight and likeness) and silver for silver (when it is equal in weight and likeness."" Then if a person gives more or demands more, it is interest."" (Muslim)"
700,"It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Khudri and Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed a person to be in charge of Khaibar. So he came to his service with very good dates. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him: ""Are all the dates that grow in Khaybar like this?"" He said: No, O Messenger of Allah! By Allah! We give other dates two sa's and (sometimes) three sa's, and these dates take one sa'. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Do not do this. Sell bad dates for a dirham, then buy good dates with a dirham.'' And he said the same about weighing items. (Bukhari and Muslim) and in Muslim it is: ""Do the same in Tul."""
701,"It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of a pile of dates that has not been measured in exchange for a fixed measure of dates. (Muslim)"
702,"It was narrated from Hazrat Muammar bin Abdullah (RA) that I used to hear the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: ""Food (grain) should be equal (in quantity) to food."" In those days, our food was barley. (Muslim)"
703,"It was narrated from Hazrat Fazla bin Ubaid (RA) that I bought a necklace for twelve dinars on the day of Khaibar. It had jewels of gold and stone. I took them apart and found more than twelve dinars of gold in them. I mentioned it to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he said: ""It should not be sold until they are separated."" (Muslim)"
704,"It is narrated from Hazrat Samura bin Jundab (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade selling an animal on loan for an animal. (All five have narrated it, and Tirmidhi and Ibn Jarood have declared it authentic.)"
705,"On the authority of Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “When you start trading in mirrors, grab the tails of oxen, love agriculture and farming, and abandon Jihad, then Allah will bring humiliation upon you.” He will not remove this (humiliation) from you until you return to your religion.”"
706,"On the authority of Hazrat Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever makes an intercession for his brother (after that), he gives him a gift and he accepts it, then he has reached the door of usury.”"
707,"It was narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr bin As, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the bribe-giver and the bribe-taker. (Narrated by Abu Dawud and Tirmidhi, and Tirmidhi said it is Sahih.)"
708,"Abu Hurairah (RAA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah said, “The performance of 'Umrah is an expiation for all the sins committed (between this 'Umrah and the previous one), and the reward for Hajj Mabrur (the one accepted by Allah or the one which was performed without doing any wrong) is nothing save Paradise.” Agreed upon."
709,"Hajj and 'Umrah."" Related by Ahmad and Ibn Majah and the wording is his. It is reported with a sound chain of narrators."
710,"Jabir bin 'Abdullah (RAA) narrated, A Bedouin came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah! Tell me about 'Umrah! Is it compulsory? He replied (ﷺ), “No (it is not compulsory), but it is better for you to perform it.” Related by Ahmad and at-Tirmidhi. Scholars are of the opinion that it is Mawquf."
711,"It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling a loan for a loan. (Narrated by Ishaq and Bazar with weak chain of transmission.)"
712,"Anas (RAA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked, ‘What is as-Sabil?’ The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) replied, ""Provision of food and means to make the journey."" Related by Ad-Daraqutni and rendered authentic by Al-Hakim."
713,"At-Tirmidhi reported the same hadith on the authority of Ibn ’Umar but with a weak chain of narrators."
714,"Ibn ’Abbas (RAA) narrated, The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came across some riders at ar-Rauha’ (a place near Madinah). He asked them, “Who are you?"" They replied, ‘Who are you?’ He replied, ""I am the Messenger of Allah."" A woman then lifted up a boy, and asked the Prophet, Will this boy be rewarded for Hajj? The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) replied, “Yes, and you too will be Rewarded.” Related by Muslim."
715,"lbn ’Abbas (RAA) narrated that ‘Al-Fadl Ibn ’Abbas was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when a woman from the tribe of Khath‘am came along, and al-Fadl started looking at her and she also started looking at him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) kept on turning al-Fadl’s face to the other side. She said, ‘O Messenger of Allah! Allah has prescribed Hajj for His servants, and it has become due on my father who is an old man, who cannot sit stable on his mount. Shall I perform Hajj on his behalf?’ The Prophet (ﷺ) replied, “Yes, you may."" This incident took place during the Farewell Pilgrimage of the Prophet (ﷺ). Agreed upon, and the wording is from Al·Bukhari’."
716,"""Yes perform Hajj on her behalf. Had there been a debt on your mother, would you have paid it or not? So, pay off her debt to Allah, for He is most deserving of settlement of His debt."" Related by Al-Bukhari."
717,"“Any minor (child) who performs Hajj must perform it again after coming of age; any slave who performs Hajj and is then freed, must perform his Hajj again."" Reported by lbn Shaibah and Al-Baihaqi. lts narrators are authoritative but scholars say that it is Mawquf."
718,"Ibn 'Abbas (RAA) narrated, ‘I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, “A man must never be alone with a woman unless there is a Mahram with her. A woman also may not travel with anyone except with a Mahram (relative).” A man stood up and asked, ‘O Messenger of Allah! My wife has gone for Hajj while I am enlisted for such and such a battle, what should I do?’ The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) replied, “Go and join your wife in Hajj."" Agreed upon, and the wording is from Muslim."
719,"Ibn 'Abbas (RAA) narrated, The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) heard a man saying, ‘O Allah! Here I am in response to Your call (saying Labbayk on behalf.. ) on behalf of Shubrumah.’ The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asked him. ""Have you performed your own Hajj?” He replied, ‘No,’ whereupon the Prophet told him, “You must perform Hajj on your own behalf first, and then perform it on behalf of Shubrumah."" Related by Abu Dawud and Ibn Majah. Ibn Hibban graded it as Sahih."
720,"“Had I said ‘yes’, it would have become a (yearly) obligation. Hajj is obligatory only once in one’s lifetime. Whatever one does over and above this is supererogatory (a voluntary act) for him."" Related by the five Imams except for at-Tirmidhi."
721,"A similar narration was also related by Muslim on the authority of Abu Hurairah."
722,"Ibn 'Abbas (RAA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) specified for the people of Madinah, DhulHulaifah (a place 540 km to the north of Makkah) as miqat. For those coming from ash-Sham (including Syria, Jordan and Palestine), he specified al-Juhfah (a place 187 km to the north-west of Makkah and close to Rabigh, where they now perform their Ihram). For those coming from Najd, he specified Qran al-Manazil, (a mountain, 94 km to the east of Makkah, overlooking 'Arafah. For those coming from Yemen, he specified Yalamlam (a mountain 54 km to the south of Makkah. These places are for the people (coming from the above specified countries) as well as for others, who pass by them on their way to perform Hajj or ’Umrah. Those living within those boundaries can assume Ihram from where they set out (for the journey), and even the residents of Makkah, their Miqat would be the place where they are staying in Makkah.’ Agreed upon."
723,"A’ishah (RAA) narrated’ ‘The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)specified for those coming from Iraq, Dhat ‘Irq (a place 94 km to the north-east of Makkah) as their Miqat.’ Related by Abu Dawud and An-Nasa’i`."
724,"Muslim related a similar narration on the authority of Jabir, but it is most probably Mawquf."
725,"Al-Bukhari reported that it was Umar, who specified Dhat 'Irq as the miqat (of those coming from Iraq)."
726,"Ibn ’Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) specified al-Aqiq (a part of `Dhat Irq) for those coming from the east.’ Related by Ahmad, Abu Dawud and An-Nasa’i."
727,"A’isha (RAA) narrated, ‘We left Madinah with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to perform the Farewell Hajj. Some of us declared Ihram to perform 'Umrah, while others declared their intentions to perform both Hajj and 'Umrah. Yet others declared their lhram to perform Hajj only. The Prophet (ﷺ) declared Ihram for Hajj only. Those who intended 'Umrah terminated their Ihram as soon as they finished the rituals of 'Umrah. Those who intended to perform Hajj only or to combine Hajj with 'Umrah, did not terminate their Ihram until the Day of Slaughtering (i.e. the day of sacrifice or ’Idul Ad-ha).’ Agreed upon."
728,"Ibn 'Umar (RAA) narrated, ‘The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to start saying the Talbiyah. (after entering the state of Ihram) from the mosque of Dhul Hulaifa (i.e. from the Miqat of Madinah). Agreed upon."
729,"“Jibril (peace be upon him) came to me and told me: ‘Command your Companions to raise their voices when saying Talbiyah.” Related by the five Imams and rendered authentic by At-Tirmidhi and Ibn Hibban."
730,"Zaid bin Thabit (RAA) narrated, ‘When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) intended to make Ihram for Hajj, he would wash, and take off his ordinary clothes (and put on his white Ihram)."" Related by At-Tirmidhi who declared it to be Hadith-Hasan."
731,"Ibn 'Umar (RAA) narrated, ‘The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about what the person who is in a state of Ihram (Muhrim) should wear. He answered, ""A person in the state of Ihram. is not allowed to wear a sewn shirt, a turban, trousers, a hooded robe, shoes or sewn slippers (Khuff), unless one is unable to find unsown slippers, then he may wear his Khuff or shoes provided one cuts them below the ankles, and you must not wear clothing that has been dyed with sweet smelling fragrance (such as saffron).” Agreed upon, and the wording is from Muslim."
732,"A’ishah (RAA) narrated, ‘I used to apply perfume to the Prophet (ﷺ) when he intended to enter the state of Ihram, before he put on his Ihram (garments). And again when he ended his state of Ihram, but before he had made Tawaf around the Ka’bah.' Agreed upon."
733,"“A Muhrim (one in the state of Ihram) must not contract marriage, nor help others contract marriage, nor get engaged to marry."" Related by Muslim."
734,"Abu Qatadah Al-Ansari (RAA) narrated concerning his hunting a zebra while he is not in a state of Ihram, that ‘Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said to Abu Qatada’s companions -who were in a state of Ihram, ""Did any one of you ask Abu Qatadah to attack the herd, or point it out to him?"" They said, ‘No.’ The Prophet then said, ""Then, you may eat what is left of the quarry."" Agreed upon."
735,"As-Sa'b bin Jath-thamah al-Laithi (RAA) narrated, ‘He presented to the Prophet (ﷺ) the meat of a zebra while he was in the area known as al-Abwa’ or Waddan. The Prophet (ﷺ) declined it, and said to him, “We declined your present only because we are in the state of Ihram."" Agreed upon."
736,"""Five kinds of animals are vicious and harmful, and they may be killed outside or inside the sacred area of Ihram (Sanctuary). These are: the scorpion, the kite, the crow, the mouse, and the rabid dog.” Agreed upon."
737,"Ibn 'Abbas (RAA) narrated, ‘The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had himself cupped while he was in the state of Ihram Agreed upon."
738,"Ka'b bin 'Ujrah (RAA) narrated, ‘I was carried to the Prophet (ﷺ) and the lice were falling over my face. He said, “I did not know that your disease is hurting you as much as what I see. Can you sacrifice a sheep?” I said, ‘No.’ He then said. “Fast for three days or feed six poor people, half a Sa’ each.” Agreed upon."
739,"Abu Hurairah (RAA) narrated, ‘When Allah, the Most High granted His Messenger (ﷺ) victory on the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (ﷺ) addressed the people, so he glorified Allah and praised Him, and said, ""Allah withheld the elephant from Makkah and empowered His Messenger and the believers over it. It has not been made lawful (i.e. fighting in it) for anyone before me, but it has been lawful for me only for a few hours on that day (of the conquest), and it will not be made lawful to anyone after me (to enter it lighting). Its wild game must not be frightened, its thorns are not to be cut. No one is allowed to pick up lost articles (Luqatah) unless he announces it (what he has found) publicly (in order to return it to the owner). If anyone has someone murdered inside its boundaries, then he has the choice of the best of two options (i.e. either to accept compensation, i.e. blood money or to retaliate). Al-'Abbas then said, ‘Except for the Idhkhar (a kind of nice smelling grass, which is used by goldsmiths and burnt in households.)"
740,"'Abdullah bin Zaid bin ’Asim (RAA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah said, ""Ibrahim declared Makkah as a Haram (Sanctuary) and made supplication for its people, and I declare Madinah to be a Haram just as Ibrahim declared Makkah as a Haram, and I made supplication for its Mudd and Sa’ (refer to hadith no. 650), just as Ibrahim made supplication for the people of Makkah."" Agreed upon."
741,"""Madinah is a Haram (Sanctuary) and its Sacred Precincts extend from ’Air to Thawr (the names of two mountains).” Related by Muslim."
742,"""Labbaika Allahumma labbaik labbaika la sharika laka labbaik, innal hamda wan-ni’mata laka wal mulk, la sharika lak (O Allah! I hasten to You. You have no partner. I hasten to You. All praise and grace is Yours and all Sovereignty too; You have no partner). When we came with him to the House (of Allah), he placed his hands on the Black Stone (Hajar al Aswad) and kis+sed it. He then started to make seven circuits (round the Ka’bah), doing ramal (trotting) in three of them and walking (at his normal pace) four other circuits. Then going to the place of Ibrahim (Maqam Ibrahim), there he prayed two rak'at. He then returned to the Black Stone (Hajar al Aswad) placed his hands on it and kissed it. Then he went out of the gate to Safa, and as he approached it, he recited: “Verily as-Safa and Marwah are among the signs appointed by Allah,""(2:158), adding, “I begin with what Allah began."" He first mounted as-Safa until he saw the House, and facing the Qiblah he declared the Oneness of Allah and glorified Him and said: ‘La ilaha illa-llah wahdahu la sharika lahu, lahul mulk wa lahul hamd, wa huwa 'ala kulli shai’in qadeer, la ilaha illa-llahu wahdahu anjaza wa'dahu, wa nas ara 'abdahu, wa hazamal ahzaba wahdah’ (There is no God but Allah, He is One, and has no partner. His is the dominion, and His is the praise and He has Power over all things. There is no God but Allah alone, Who fulfilled His promise, helped His servant and defeated the confederates alone."") He said these words three times making supplications in between. He then descended and walked towards Marwah, and when his feet touched the bottom of the valley, he ran; and when he began to ascend, he walked (at his normal pace) until he reached Marwah. There he did as he had done at Safa…. 
When it was the day of Tarwiyah (8th of Dhul-Hijjah) they went to Mina and put on the Ihram for Hajj and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) rode his mount, and there he led the Dhur (noon), ‘Asr (afternoon), Maghrib (sunset), ‘Isha and Fajr (dawn) prayers. He then waited a little until the sun had risen, and commanded that a tent be pitched at Namirah (close to Arafat). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), continued on until he came to Arafah and he found that the tent had been pitched for him at Namirah. There he got down until the sun had passed its meridian; he commanded that al-Qaswa’ be brought and saddled for him, then he came to the bottom of the valley, and addressed the people with the well-known sermon Khutbat al-Wada (the Farewell Sermon). Then the Adhan was pronounced and later on the Iqamah and the Prophet led the Dhuhr (noon) prayer. Then another Iqamah was pronounced and the Prophet led the Asr (afternoon) prayer and he observed no other prayer in between the two. The Messenger of Allah then mounted his camel and came to the place where he was to stay. He made his she-camel, al-Qaswa turn towards the rocky side, with the pedestrian path lying in front of him. He faced the Qiblah, and stood there until the sun set, and the yellow light diminished somewhat, and the disc of the sun totally disappeared. He pulled the nose string of al-Qaswa’ so forcefully that its head touched the saddle (in order to keep her under perfect control), and pointing with his right hand, advised the people to be moderate (in speed) saying: “O people! Calmness! Calmness!"" Whenever he passed over an elevated tract of land, he slightly loosened the nose-string of his camel until she climbed up. This is how he reached al-Muzdalifah. There he led the Maghrib (sunset) and Isha prayers with one Adhan, and two lqamas, and did not pray any optional prayers in between them. The Messenger of Allah then lay down until dawn and then offered the Fajr (dawn) prayer with an Adhan and an Iqamah when the morning light was clear. He again mounted al-Qaswa’, and when he came to Al-Mash‘ar Al-Haram (The Sanctuary Landmark, which is a small mountain at al-Muzdalifah) he faced the Qiblah, and supplicated to Allah, Glorified Him, and pronounced His Uniqueness and Oneness, and kept standing until the daylight was very clear. Then he set off quickly before the sun rose, until he came to the bottom of the valley of Muhassir where he urged her (al·Qaswa’) a little. He followed the middle road, which comes out at the greatest Jamarah (one of the three stoning sites called Jamrat-ul ‘Aqabah), he came to Jamarah which is near the tree. At this he threw seven small pebbles, saying, Allahu Akbar` while throwing each of them in a manner in which small pebbles are thrown (holding them with his fingers) and this he did while at the bottom of the valley. He then went to the Place of sacrifice, and sacrificed sixty-three (camels) with his own hand (he brought 100 camels with him and he asked ’Ali to sacrifice the rest). The Messenger of Allah again rode and came to the House (of Allah), where he performed Tawaf al-Ifada and offered the Dhuhr prayer at Makkah….’ Muslim transmitted this hadith through a very long narration describing the full details of the Hajj of the Prophet"
743,"Khuzaimah bin Thabit (RAA) narrated, ‘When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) finished his Talbiyah whether in Hajj or 'Umrah, he would ask Allah for His good pleasure and acceptance and ask Him for Paradise, and would seek refuge in Him from Hell.’ Related by Ash-Shafi'i with a weak chain of narrators."
744,"""I have offered my sacrifice here (at Mina) and all of Mina is a place for slaughtering, so sacrifice where you are staying (at Mina). And I have stopped here (at Arafat) and all of Arafat is a stopping place (for the Day of Arafat on the 9th of Dhul-Hijjah). And I have stood here, and all of Jam' (meaning al·Muzdalifah) is a place for standing.” Related by Muslim."
745,"A’ishah (RAA) narrated, ‘When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to Makkah, he entered from its higher side (a place now called al-Mu'alla gate) and went out from its lower side (now called Kuda).’ Agreed upon."
746,"Whenever Ibn 'Umar (RAA) came to Makkah he would spend the night at Dhi Tuwa valley (near Makkah), and in the morning he would bathe. ‘Ibn 'Umar used to say that this is what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), used to do.’ Agreed upon."
747,"Ibn 'Abbas (RAA) narrated that he used to kiss the Black Stone and prostrate himself on it. Related by Al-Hakim and Al-Baihaqi."
748,"Ibn 'Abbas (RAA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded them to trot for three circuits and walk (with a normal pace) for four circuits, between the two corners (The Black Stone and the Yemeni corner). Agreed upon."
749,"The Black Stone and the Yemeni corner) Related by Muslim."
750,"'Umar (RAA) narrated that he kissed the Black Stone and said, ‘I know that you are a stone and can neither benefit anyone nor harm anyone. Had I not seen Allah’s Messenger(ﷺ) kissing you, I would not have kissed you.’ Agreed upon."
751,"Abu At-Tufail (RAA) narrated, ‘l saw Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) making Tawaf round the Ka'bah and he was touching the corner (of the Black Stone) with a stick that he had with him and then kissing the stick.’ Related by Muslim."
752,"Ya'li bin Umaiyah (RAA) narrated, The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made the Tawaf while wearing a green Yemeni mantle, bringing it up from under his right armpit while covering the left shoulder.’ Related by the five Imams except for An-Nasa’i. At-Tirmidhi graded it as Sahih"
753,"Anas (RAA) narrated, ‘When we assumed Ihram (for Hajj or 'Umrah) some of us raised their voices with Talbiyah and nobody objected to that, and others raised their voices with Takbir and no one objected to that (which means that saying Allahu Akbar ‘Allah is the Greatest’, or reciting the Talbiyah are both acceptable during Ihram).’ Agreed upon."
754,"Ibn ‘Abbas (RAA) narrated, ‘The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me at night from al-Muzdalifah (to Mina) with the weak members of his family (women and children).’ Agreed upon."
755,"A’ishah (RAA) narrated, ‘Saudah(the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ) asked his permission, on the night of al-Muzdalifah, to leave earlier (to Mina as she was a heavy and slow woman.’ The Prophet (ﷺ) gave her permission.’ Agreed upon."
756,"Ibn 'Abbas (RAA) narrated, ‘The Messenger of Allah said to us, ""Do not throw the pebbles at Jamrah al-‘Aqabah until sunrise.” Related by the five Imams except An-Nasa’i, but with a disconnected chain of narrators."
757,"A’ishah (RAA) narrated, ‘The Prophet sent Umm Salamah on the night of the 10th (before the day of the Sacrifice) and she threw her pebbles before dawn, after which she returned to Makkah to perform Tawaf.’’ Related by Abu Dawud."
758,"“Anyone who offered this prayer -at al-Muzdalifah- along with us, and waited with us until we returned to Mina, and he stayed at 'Arafat (on the 9th ) before that by night or day, he would have completed the prescribed duties of Hajj."" Related by the five Imams. At-Tirmidhi and Ibn Khuzaimah graded it as Sahih."
759,"'Umar (RAA) narrated, ‘The pagans did not use to depart from Muzdalifah until the sun had risen, and they would say, ‘Let the sun shine on Thabir (the highest mountain in Makkah). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) contradicted them and departed from Muzdalifah before sunrise.' Related by Al-Bukhari."
760,"Ibn 'Abbas and Usamah bin Zaid (RAA) narrated, The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) kept on reciting Talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat-ul ‘Aqabah..’ Related by Al-Bukhari."
761,"On the authority of Hazrat Abu Rafi', the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The neighbor has more rights because of his proximity (neighborhood)."""
762,"'Abdullah bin Masud (RAA) narrated that he kept the Ka'bah on his left and Mina on his right and threw the seven pebbles of Jamrat-ul ‘Aqabah. He then said, ‘This is the location where the one on whom surah al-Baqarah. (surah no. 2) was revealed (i e. the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)).’ Agreed upon."
763,"Jabir bin 'Abdullah (RAA) narrated, ‘The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) threw Jamrat—ul 'Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice (the 9th of Dhul Hijjah) in the forenoon. On the following days he threw them when the sun had passed its meridian.’ Related by Muslim."
764,"Ibn 'Umar (RAA) narrated that he used to throw the pebbles of al-Jamrat ud-Duniya (the Jamrah near to the Khaif mosque) with seven small pebbles, and would recite Takbir when throwing each pebble. Then he would go ahead until he reached the bottom of the valley, where he would stand for quite a long time facing the direction of the Qiblah, and raising his hands, while supplicating Allah. Then he went and threw seven pebbles at the second Jamrah(al-Jamarah al·Wosta) while saying Allahu Akbar with each throw. He would then turn to the left of the bottom of the valley, stand there facing the Qiblah and supplicating to Allah with his hands raised. Then he went to Jamrat-ul Aqabah, threw seven pebbles at it, uttering the Takbir with each throw. After that he left and did not pause. He would then say, ‘I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) doing like this.’ Related by Al-Bukhari."
765,"“May Allah bless those who shaved."" The Companions asked him, ‘O Allah’s Messenger, what about those who cut their hair short?’ They repeated their question twice (and each time he repeated his saying, ‘May Allah bless those who shaved.’) On the third time, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) then said, “And (may Allah bless) those who cut their hair short."" Agreed upon."
766,"“There is no harm, go and slaughter your animal."" Another man asked, ‘l slaughtered the animal before I threw the pebbles? Prophet (ﷺ) said: “There is no harm, go and throw your pebbles."" The narrator said: ""Whoever asked the Prophet (ﷺ) about anything done before or after the other he told him ""No harm done. Go and do (whatever you missed)."" Agreed upon."
767,"Al-Maisur bin Makhramah (RAA) narrated, ‘The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sacrificed his animal before he shaved and commanded his companions to do so.’ Related by Al-Bukhari."
768,"""When one of you threw the pebbles and shaved his hair, everything including perfume becomes lawful for him except women (i.e. sexual intercourse).” Related by Ahmad and Abu Dawud with a weak chain of narrators."
769,"""Women (pilgrims) do not have to shave (their heads); they may only shorten their hair."" Related by Abu Dawud with a good chain of narrators."
770,"Ibn ‘Umar (RAA) narrated that ‘Al-’Abbas bin 'Abdul Muttalib asked permission from the Prophet (ﷺ) to stay at Makkah during the nights of Mina in order to provide drinking water (from Zamzam) to the pilgrims, and the Prophet (ﷺ) allowed him.’ Agreed Upon."
771,"‘Asim bin ‘Adi (RAA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) excused the herdsmen of camels from sleeping at Mina and asked them to throw pebbles on the day of sacrifice (i.e. throw Jamrat-ul ‘Aqabah and they do not have to spend the night at Mina), and then to throw the pebbles of the next day and the day after (i.e. of the 11th and the 12th combined (on the 12th ), and then throw pebbles again on the 13th Related by the five Imams. At-Tirmidhi and Ibn Hibban graded it as Sahih."
772,"Abu Bakrah (RAA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a sermon to us on the Day of Nahr (sacrifice) (and the narrator mentioned the sermon.).’ Agreed upon."
773,"Sarra’ bint Nabhan (RAA) narrated ‘The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a sermon to us on the second day of sacrifice, ‘Yaum ar-Ru’us’ (11th of Dhul -Hijjah) and said, ""Is this not the middle of the days of Tashriq?” Related by Abu Dawud."
774,"Ibn 'Umar (RAA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Give the hired worker his wages before his sweat dries."" Related by Ibn Majah.

On this topic, there are also narrations from Abu Hurairah (RAA), related by Abu Ya'la and al-Baihaqi, and from Jabir (RAA), related by at-Tabarani, but all of them are weak."
775,"Ibn 'Abbas (RAA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not trot during the seven circuits made in the final Tawaf when he returned to Makkah.’ Related by the five Imams except at-Tirmidhi. Al-Hakim graded it as Sahih."
776,"Anas (RAA), narrated, 'The Messenger of Allah rested for a while at al-Muhassab (a valley opening at al-Abtah between Makkah and Mina) prayed Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib and 'Isha prayers after which he rode to the Ka’bah and made Tawaf.’ Related by Al·Bukhari."
777,"A’ishah (RAA) narrated that she did not use to do that i.e. rest at al-Muhassab and said, ‘The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) rested at al-Muhassab, because it was easier to stop there and depart from (i.e. it is not a Sunnah to rest there`). Related by Muslim."
778,"Ibn 'Abbas (RAA) narrated, ‘People were commanded to make the Tawaf round the Ka’bah their last rite;(Farewell Tawaf but the menstruating women were excused from it.’ Agreed upon."
779,"""Offering prayer in my mosque (in Madinah) is better than one thousand prayers elsewhere, save for those offered prayer in al-Masjid al-Haram (in Makkah). And prayer offered in al-Masjid al-Haram is better than prayer offered in my mosque by one hundred prayers."" Related by Ahmad and Ibn Hibban graded it as Sahih."
780,"Ibn ‘Abbas (RAA) narrated, ‘When the Prophet (ﷺ) was prevented from performing ‘Umrah (by Quraish) he shaved his head, had intercourse with his wives and slaughtered his animal. The next year he performed ‘Umrah to make up for the year that he had missed.’ Related by Al-Bukhari."
781,"A’ishah (RAA) narrated, 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went to visit. Duba’ah bint Az-Zubair bin 'Abdul Muttalib. She said to him, ‘O Messenger of Allah I have made the intention to perform Hajj but I am suffering from an illness.’ He said to her, “Perform Hajj but set a condition that you shall be relieved of the Ihram whenever you are prevented (due to illness, etc.).” Agreed upon."
782,"Hazrat Alqamah bin Wail narrates from his father Hazrat Wail (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him a piece of land as a manor in the presence of death. (Narrated by Abu Dawud and Tirmidhi, and Ibn Hibban declared it authentic.)"
783,"It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) granted Hazrat Zubair (RA) a land equal to the race of his horse as a jagir, so he ran the horse until it stopped, then he threw his whip forward. He said: ""Give him (Zubair) the land as far as the whip reaches."""
784,"There is a hadith on the authority of a Sahabi, may God be pleased with him, who said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a campaign, and I heard him say: ""All people share in three things: grass, water, and fire."""
785,"On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When a person dies, all his deeds are cut off except for three deeds.”"
786,"Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that (my father) Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) got some land in Khyber, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to seek advice and said: O Messenger of Allah! I have acquired some land in Khyber. It is so exquisite and precious that I have never found such a land before. (I want to give it in charity. What do you say?) He said: ""If you want, dedicate its original (area) and give its fruits as a charity."" Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) says that Hazrat Umar (RA) gave that land as a charity on the condition that its original (area) will not be sold, nor be given as an inheritance, nor will it be given away, but it will be used as a way to free the poor, the relatives, and the slaves. He gave charity for travelers and guests on the way. (And also bequeathed that) its administrator and caretaker can eat according to the known method and can also feed friends and associates. But don't hoard wealth. (Bukhari and Muslim, these words are from Muslim.) And in a tradition of Bukhari, it is said: He gave the original as Sadaqah (waqf) which will not be sold or given away, but its production will be spent in the way of God."
787,"There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, who says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) to collect charity. (The narrator) narrated the complete hadith and it is in it: (He said:) “As for Khalid (RA), he has dedicated his armor and war equipment, everything in the way of Allah.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
788,"It is narrated from Hazrat Nu'man bin Basheer (RA) that his father (Bashir) brought him to the service of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and said, ""I have given my personal slave to this son of mine."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Have you sacrificed all your children in this way?"" He said: No! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Then return it.” And the words of a hadith are: My father came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to make him witness about my charity (Hiba). He said: ""Have you done this to all your children?"" He replied: No! He said: ""Fear Allah and do justice between your children."" So my father returned and he took back that charity (Hiba). (Bukhari and Muslim) And there is a hadith of Muslim: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""Then make someone other than me as a witness on this."" Then he said: ""Do you like that all your children treat you equally well?"" He said: Why not! He said: ""Then don't do that."""
789,"It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The one who vomits and takes it back is like a dog that vomits and then licks its own vomit."""
790,"On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar and Hazrat Ibn Abbas, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""It is not permissible for a Muslim man to give a gift and take it back, except for a father who gives to his children."" (It can be taken back by him).” (Narrated by Ahmad and Al-Charu, and authenticated by Tirmidhi, Ibn Hibban and Al-Hakim.)"
791,"There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Aisha, she says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to accept gifts and would give some favors in return. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
792,"There is a hadith on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that a man donated a camel to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace. He gave him some gift in return and said: ""Are you satisfied?"" He said: No! Then, with some more mercy, he asked: ""Are you happy now?"" He again said no. Then he asked him more boldly: ""Are you ready now?"" He said yes! (It was narrated by Ahmad and Ibn Hibban called it Sahih.)"
793,"It is narrated from Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Umrah belongs to the one who has been entrusted with it."" Do not waste them because the person who gives Umrah to someone, then that Umrah belongs to the one to whom it is given, 'in life and after death' and for his descendants after his death. But when he says that it is for you as long as you live, then he (Umrah) will turn back to his giver. It is in the tradition of Abu Dawud and Nasa'i: ""Do not give a gift in the manner of Rabi'a and Umrah."" Therefore, if a person is given an area or an Umrah, it is for his heirs."
794,"It was narrated from Hazrat Umar that I gave a man a horse to ride in the way of Allah. It disabled him. I thought he was going to sell it cheap. I asked the Messenger of Allah (may peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it (can I buy it?), so he said: ""Even if he gives it (the horse) to you for one dirham, do not buy it."" (The narrator) narrated the complete hadith. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
795,"On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Give gifts to each other, it will create mutual love."""
796,"It is narrated from Hazrat Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Exchange gifts to each other, because a gift removes malice and resentment."""
797,"On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Muslim women! A neighbor should never despise his neighbor (for sending a gift), even if it (the gift) is a goat's hoof."" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
798,"It is narrated from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever gives something, he is more entitled to it, until he is repaid."""
799,"There is a hadith on the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a date palm that had fallen on the road, and he said: ""If I had not feared that it would be for charity, I would have eaten it."" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
800,"On the authority of Hazrat Zayd bin Khalid Jahni, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about Laqta. He said: ""Know its bag (or the thing in which it is) and its strap"" then keep announcing it throughout the year. If its real owner comes, hand it over to him, otherwise do whatever you want.” Then he asked about the lost goats. He said: ""Is it yours or your brother's or the wolf's?"" Then he asked about the lost camels. He said: ""What does that concern you?"" He has his water and his shoes. He will come to the ghat and drink water and eat the leaves of the trees until his owner reaches him.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
801,"On the authority of Hazrat Zayd bin Khalid Jahni, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever shelters a lost animal with him, he himself is misguided until he announces it."" (Narrated by Muslim)."
802,"On the authority of Hazrat Ayaz bin Hamar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever finds a piece of cloth, he should make two fair men witness to it, and remember his bowl and headgear."" Then he should not hide it. If its real owner comes, he is more entitled to it. If it does not come, then it is the property of Allah, He gives it to whomever He wills.”"
803,"Hazrat Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman Taymi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the Hajjs to carry the laqta. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
804,"On the authority of Hazrat Muqadam bin Maad Yakarb, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Listen! An animal that is crushed by beasts, a domestic donkey, and anything that is picked up from a dhimmi's property is not halal unless he (the dhimmi) is free from it."" (Narrated by Abu Dawood.)"
805,"On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Give the fixed shares (of the inheritance) to those who are entitled to them, then whatever remains is for the nearest male (heir) of the deceased."" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
806,"On the authority of Hazrat Osama bin Zayd, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""A Muslim cannot inherit from an infidel and an infidel cannot inherit from a Muslim."" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
807,"Hazrat Ibn Masoud (RA) has a hadith about daughter, granddaughter and sister that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) decided about it that the daughter will get half (half share) and the granddaughter will get six (sixth) to fulfill two-thirds, then whatever is left will be the sister's."" (Bukhari)"
808,"It is narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Followers of two different religions cannot be heirs to each other."""
809,"It is narrated from Hazrat Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: My grandson has died. How much is my share in his inheritance? He said: ""You will get a sixth (sixth)."" Then when he started to leave, he called him and said: ""There is another sixth for you."" Then when he started to leave, he called him and said: ""The last sixth is provision for you."" Not hearsay.)"
810,"Hazrat (Abdullah) Ibn Burida narrated from his father (Burida) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned a sixth share to Jeddah (grandmother) when there was no mother before her. (Narrated by Abu Dawud and Nasa'i, Ibn Khuzimah and Ibn Jarood declared it Sahih, and Ibn Adi declared it strong.)"
811,"On the authority of Hazrat Muqadam bin Maadikarb, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The maternal uncle will be the heir of the one who has no heir (among the Companions of the Furuz or Asabat)."""
812,"Hazrat Abu Umamah bin Sahl (RA) narrates that Hazrat Umar (RA) wrote to me for Hazrat Abu Ubaidah (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (SAW) said: “Whoever has no master, Allah and His Messenger are his master, and whoever has no heir, his maternal uncle is his heir.” .)"
813,"On the authority of Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""When a new-born child utters a sound, it is made an heir."""
814,"Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrates from his father (Shu'aib) and he (Shu'aib) from his grandfather, he says, ""The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The murderer does not get anything from the inheritance of the deceased."""
815,"On the authority of Hazrat Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: ""Whatever the father or son collects, it is for his Asbah, whoever that (Asbah) may be."""
816,"On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Wala' is a relation like the relation of descent, which cannot be sold or given."""
817,"Hazrat Abu Qalaba narrates from Hazrat Anas that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The most knowledgeable of you is Zayd bin Thabit (may God be pleased with him) who is an expert on inheritance."""
818,"On the authority of Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""It is not proper for a Muslim to intend to make a will about something he owns, but he spends two nights in a state where he does not have a written will."" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
819,"On the authority of Hazrat Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, he says: I said: O Messenger of Allah! I am a wealthy man and my only heir is my daughter. So should I give two-thirds of the wealth in charity? He said: ""No."" I asked again: Shall I give half of my wealth in charity? He said: ""No."" I asked for the third time: So can I give one-third of my wealth in charity? He said: ""Yes! But one third is too much. It is better for you to leave your heirs rich than to leave them needy and to spread their hands in front of the people.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
820,"It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha that a person came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! My mother died suddenly and left no will. My opinion about her is that if she had a conversation, she would (definitely) give charity. Will he be rewarded if I give charity on his behalf? He said: ""Yes."" (Bukhari and Muslim) These words are from Muslim."
821,"It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Umamah Bahli (may God be pleased with him) that I heard the Messenger of God (may God bless him and grant him peace) say: “Allah has given every rightful person his right, so there is no will for an heir.” What is the hadith from and this addition has also been quoted at the end of it: ""Unless his heirs wish."""
822,"On the authority of Hazrat Muadh bin Jabal, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Allah has favored you by allowing you to bequeath one-third of your wealth at the time of death, so that your good deeds may increase."" Allah knows best."
823,"Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrates from his father (Shuaib) and he (Shuaib) from his grandfather (Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is entrusted with something, there is no responsibility on him.” (Narrated by Ibn Majah and its chain of transmission is weak.)"
